  "correctness_argument": "YeastPhenome releases a medium's composition inside the media field of a column header, and the loader stored it inside Media.name, which media_identity drops. Measured over the 524,682 records of the v1.0 pin (experiments/database/scripts/media_name_composition_scan.py, results media_name_composition_scan.json): 28 released tokens reached 13 distinct stored names and 8 distinct media identities; 53,951 records sat on a served environment node reached from a DIFFERENT released medium; and the 4,837 record pairs that remained in yeastphenome's expected_duplicated_pairs allowance after lane W's aerobicity fix were Galardini 2019's nitrogen-free arm ('SD + His + Leu + Lys + Ura, -N', condition 'standard') counted as repeats of its own control ('SD + His + Leu + Lys + Ura (2)', condition 'standard'). An instruction to aggregate the declared duplicates would have destroyed 4,837 measurements, which is the aerobicity failure mode of lane W one level down. Reading the token into typed fields fixes the other statements with no schema change (a named dropout is Media.dropouts, a carbon source or a buffer or a vehicle or a selection agent or a supplement is a Media.components line at its stated dose), and the two role-level statements cannot be expressed at all: 'SC (-C)' and 'SD ..., -N' name a nutrient CLASS the curation declares absent and never name the compound removed, so dropouts (list[Compound]) would need a Compound standing for a class, which is principle 5's free-string-for-a-closed-vocabulary defect. A medium whose composition is LISTED states such an absence by having no component in that role, which is how M9_NOCARBON_WETMORE2015 and the other eleven no-carbon library objects say it; a medium whose composition is not entered cannot, because components=[] already means 'composition not yet entered'. Media.dropout_roles is that statement in the closed vocabulary MediaComponentRole already holds, and it is the same 'omitted is distinguishable from not yet listed' rule Media.dropouts exists for, one level up. It is additive and optional-by-construction (default empty) and carries exclude_if=lambda v: not v, so a medium that states no role-level omission serializes to EXACTLY the bytes it did before the field existed and every content-addressed id over it is unchanged (the Environment.growth_phase precedent; measured: the ten adapter tests that pin the yeast node lists and the content-addressed experiment, genotype and publication ids failed without it and pass with it). Its validators only refuse contradictions: a repeated role, and a role declared omitted while a component fills it (the ProvenanceGapMixin invariant that a value and a declared absence cannot coexist). It joins MEDIA_OPTIONAL_IDENTITY_FIELDS rather than MEDIA_IDENTITY_FIELDS, so it is projected only when non-empty and every medium that states no role-level omission hashes exactly as it did before the field existed: verified by test_a_role_level_dropout_is_identity_and_an_empty_one_changes_no_id, and by the yeastphenome media identities, where the 8 pre-fix identities become 28 with no two tokens sharing one and no record moved onto an identity it did not have a right to. The same record carries the identity half of lane W's second finding: Environment.growth_phase was in no identity projection, served or verifying, although CultureGrowthPhase's own definition separates the harvest moment (a property of the sample) from a culture HELD in a phase AS the condition, which is what the field is. It joins ENVIRONMENT_OPTIONAL_IDENTITY_FIELDS, which is consistent with its construction (exclude_if=lambda v: v is None, so an environment that states no phase serializes exactly as it did before the field existed) and keeps every existing environment id unchanged. Measured effect on duplicate accounting: 4 of 181 readable dev stores state a growth phase, all Schmidt 2016, 2 stationary environments each, and dropping the field from the projection merges 0 of them, because both stationary arms also differ in duration_hours; so no store's duplicate count moves today and the projection is correct for the first release that holds a phase at one duration. No stored record is dropped or merged anywhere: the yeastphenome record total is 524,682 before and after.",
  "measurement_type_decision": false,
