  "alternatives_rejected": [
    {
      "alternative": "Put the role-level omission in Media.dropouts as a Compound named for the class ('carbon source', 'nitrogen source')",
      "why_rejected": "A Compound is a molecule keyed by an InChIKey; a Compound whose name is a nutrient class is a free string standing for a closed vocabulary, which principle 5 refuses, and it would join nothing in the compound table."
    },
    {
      "alternative": "Substitute the library SC object for the token and express the omission with dropout(), as Hillenmeyer 2008 does",
      "why_rejected": "It imports a 30-component recipe, with two other papers' quotes, into a record whose secondary curation states only the label 'SC'; the loader's standing treatment is that no library object is substituted for a released token and base_medium carries the join. The dropout() route is right where the base recipe is the source's own, and it is still available to any loader whose source prints one."
    },
    {
      "alternative": "Express 'SC (-C)' as an EnvironmentPhysicalPerturbation of PhysicalFactor.carbon_source with no magnitude",
      "why_rejected": "A medium without a carbon source is a property of the medium, not an edit applied on top of it; the Hillenmeyer comment in media.py states exactly this for a named-nutrient dropout ('a derived medium, not an EnvironmentPhysicalPerturbation'), and the column's own carbon dose IS already a perturbation, so the two facts would be welded into one slot."
    },
    {
      "alternative": "Declare the omission with a ProvenanceGap on Media.components",
      "why_rejected": "A gap requires its field to be None (ProvenanceGapMixin), and components is a list that defaults to empty, so the gap would be refused; and a gap says 'we could not find the value', where the source states the value positively."
    },
    {
      "alternative": "Add dropout_roles to MEDIA_IDENTITY_FIELDS (the required tuple) rather than the optional one",
      "why_rejected": "The canonical JSON would gain a key on every medium, changing every served environment node id for a statement that no existing medium makes; projecting it only when non-empty says the same thing about identity and moves only the media that state a role-level omission."
    },
    {
      "alternative": "Leave Environment.growth_phase out of the identity projection, since it is None on every store measured",
      "why_rejected": "It is the condition on the records that set it (CultureGrowthPhase's own definition: a culture HELD in a phase, as against the harvest moment, which lives on the phenotype), so two records differing only in it are two conditions; the measured null today is a property of the stores, not of the field, and the next release that holds a phase at one duration would merge."
    },
    {
      "alternative": "Keep yeastphenome's expected_duplicated_pairs at 4,837 and let the loader aggregate them",
      "why_rejected": "They are not repeats: they are a nitrogen-starvation arm and its control. Aggregating would destroy 4,837 released measurements, which the owner's rule (the data is the data) forbids."
    },
    {
      "alternative": "Let the empty list serialize, as components and dropouts do",
      "why_rejected": "Every medium's dump would gain 'dropout_roles': [], which changes the content-addressed experiment id of every record in every store for a field that says nothing; exclude_if keeps the bytes identical and the statement is still typed where it is made. Measured: ten adapter tests pinning the yeast node lists and the content ids fail without exclude_if and pass with it."
    }
  ],
